1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,350
You go online to buy one thing.

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,436
You leave with four.

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,867
And somehow, it felt like you saved money.

4
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:07,498
That's not bad luck.

5
00:00:07,518 --> 00:00:08,520
It's design.

6
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,738
Shops test prices, buttons,

7
00:00:10,758 --> 00:00:13,335
colours and timers on millions of people.

8
00:00:13,355 --> 00:00:15,351
Your brain is the thing they're testing.

9
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:18,122
And here's the part nobody tells you.

10
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,749
Once you can see the tricks,

11
00:00:20,769 --> 00:00:22,183
most of them stop working.

12
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:24,198
Here are seven of them,

13
00:00:24,218 --> 00:00:25,292
and how to beat each one.

14
00:00:25,312 --> 00:00:26,280
Let's begin.

15
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:27,630
One.

16
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,374
The price that ends in nine.

17
00:00:30,367 --> 00:00:33,647
€9.99 feels much closer to nine than to ten.

18
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:35,366
Your brain reads the first digit,

19
00:00:35,386 --> 00:00:36,748
and mostly stops there.

20
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,560
In one experiment,

21
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,607
a clothing catalogue raised the price

22
00:00:40,627 --> 00:00:43,670
of a dress from $34 to $39.

23
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:45,480
It sold about a third more.

24
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:49,444
At $44, it sold the same as at $34.

25
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:50,799
The fix:

26
00:00:50,819 --> 00:00:52,435
round prices up in your head.

27
00:00:52,455 --> 00:00:54,735
€9.99 is ten euros.

28
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:56,771
€49.95 is fifty.

29
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:58,307
Two.

30
00:00:58,327 --> 00:00:59,195
The decoy.

31
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:02,440
A magazine once offered three options.

32
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,660
Online only:

33
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:04,870
$59.

34
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:05,120
Print only:

35
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,965
$125.

36
00:01:06,985 --> 00:01:07,635
Print and online:

37
00:01:07,655 --> 00:01:10,499
$125.

38
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,670
Nobody picks print only.

39
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:13,610
It's there to make the

40
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:15,079
bundle look like a steal.

41
00:01:15,933 --> 00:01:17,663
In a famous class experiment,

42
00:01:17,683 --> 00:01:20,267
84% of students chose the bundle.

43
00:01:20,533 --> 00:01:22,003
When the decoy was removed,

44
00:01:22,023 --> 00:01:25,328
68% chose the cheap online option instead.

45
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,407
The fix:

46
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:27,794
when you see three prices,

47
00:01:27,814 --> 00:01:29,840
ask which one is only there to push you.

48
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:31,437
Then compare the other two.

49
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:33,019
Three.

50
00:01:33,039 --> 00:01:34,270
The fake countdown.

51
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,033
Only two left.

52
00:01:36,053 --> 00:01:37,758
Offer ends in nine minutes.

53
00:01:37,778 --> 00:01:39,682
Someone in Paris just bought this.

54
00:01:40,067 --> 00:01:41,748
Urgency switches off the slow,

55
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,349
careful part of your brain.

56
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:46,102
In a check published in 2023,

57
00:01:46,122 --> 00:01:51,037
EU consumer authorities looked at 399 online shops.

58
00:01:51,057 --> 00:01:54,411
148 used at least one manipulative trick.

59
00:01:54,767 --> 00:01:57,695
42 of them had countdown timers that were fake.

60
00:01:58,367 --> 00:01:58,826
The fix:

61
00:01:58,846 --> 00:02:00,607
if a timer says hurry, wait.

62
00:02:00,627 --> 00:02:02,793
A real deal survives a night of sleep.

63
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:04,209
Four.

64
00:02:04,229 --> 00:02:05,464
The fake discount.

65
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:08,318
Was €199.

66
00:02:08,338 --> 00:02:10,088
Now €99.

67
00:02:10,108 --> 00:02:10,338
Half price!

68
00:02:10,358 --> 00:02:14,083
But was it ever really €199?

69
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,295
A high before price is an anchor.

70
00:02:16,315 --> 00:02:18,288
It makes the new price feel small.

71
00:02:19,033 --> 00:02:21,228
In the EU, since 2022,

72
00:02:21,248 --> 00:02:23,600
a shop announcing a discount has to compare it

73
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:26,466
with its lowest price in the previous thirty days.

74
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:29,558
So check that small line, or a price tracker,

75
00:02:29,578 --> 00:02:31,242
before you believe the percentage.

76
00:02:32,433 --> 00:02:32,742
Five.

77
00:02:32,762 --> 00:02:33,732
Free shipping.

78
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:36,402
Shipping costs €4.90.

79
00:02:36,422 --> 00:02:38,207
It's free above €50.

80
00:02:38,227 --> 00:02:40,449
Your basket is at €38.

81
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:43,682
So you add a €15 thing you didn't plan to buy,

82
00:02:43,702 --> 00:02:45,495
to save €4.90.

83
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:49,522
You just spent €10 more to avoid paying €4.90.

84
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:50,314
The fix:

85
00:02:50,334 --> 00:02:51,320
pay the shipping,

86
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:53,209
or wait until you really need more.

87
00:02:54,533 --> 00:02:54,823
Six.

88
00:02:54,843 --> 00:02:56,289
Buy now, pay later.

89
00:02:57,233 --> 00:02:59,507
Four payments of €25 feel

90
00:02:59,527 --> 00:03:01,863
lighter than one payment of €100.

91
00:03:01,883 --> 00:03:03,821
It's the same €100.

92
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:08,976
One large study of US bank data found that once people start using buy now,

93
00:03:08,996 --> 00:03:11,667
pay later, their total spending goes up,

94
00:03:11,687 --> 00:03:12,967
and stays up for months.

95
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:19,695
New EU consumer credit rules, due to apply from November 2026, bring most buy now,

96
00:03:19,715 --> 00:03:21,695
pay later under credit rules,

97
00:03:21,715 --> 00:03:23,583
with checks on whether you can afford it.

98
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:24,667
The fix:

99
00:03:24,687 --> 00:03:25,992
if you can't pay for it today,

100
00:03:26,012 --> 00:03:27,854
you probably can't afford it today.

101
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:29,524
Seven.

102
00:03:29,544 --> 00:03:30,552
The store map.

103
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:33,280
Milk and bread are usually at the back.

104
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:35,803
To reach them, you walk past everything else.

105
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,943
And the sweets wait at the checkout,

106
00:03:37,963 --> 00:03:40,348
right where you stand still with nothing to do.

107
00:03:41,167 --> 00:03:43,575
England even banned less healthy snacks from

108
00:03:43,595 --> 00:03:46,450
the checkouts of larger stores in 2022.

109
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:47,136
The fix:

110
00:03:47,156 --> 00:03:47,964
shop with a list,

111
00:03:47,984 --> 00:03:49,689
and walk straight to what's on it.

112
00:03:50,833 --> 00:03:52,012
Final message.

113
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,670
Some of these tricks are banned.

114
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:56,280
Most are perfectly legal.

115
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,974
They're just very good design.

116
00:03:58,667 --> 00:03:59,747
Round prices up.

117
00:03:59,767 --> 00:03:59,997
Spot the decoy.

118
00:04:00,017 --> 00:04:01,384
Ignore the timer.

119
00:04:01,404 --> 00:04:03,092
Check the real old price.

120
00:04:03,112 --> 00:04:03,342
Pay the shipping.

121
00:04:03,362 --> 00:04:04,464
Pay in full.

122
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:05,276
Bring a list.

123
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,515
Your brain isn't stupid.

124
00:04:07,535 --> 00:04:08,791
It's just being tested by

125
00:04:08,811 --> 00:04:10,379
people who do this all day.

126
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:13,687
This is education, not financial advice.

127
00:04:13,707 --> 00:04:15,467
If this helped, subscribe.

128
00:04:15,487 --> 00:04:15,717
Next up:

129
00:04:15,737 --> 00:04:18,760
how to save money so easily it feels illegal.
